			Parallel Computation Modeller


	THERMO is a "thermodynamic computation" simulator for a series of
stochastic energy-minimization search algorithms.  On a set of progressively
more intractable "problem terrains," users can implement and refine: 
(i) depth vs. breadth-first search;  (ii) global vs local minima
discrimination;  and, finally, (iii) simulated annealing "temperature-schedule"
algorithms.  

	Equipment:  THERMO requires full IBM compatibility with either an EGA
or VGA color graphics card and monitor.  (Performs best on 80286-based PCs 
and up.) 

	THERMO requires no special installation procedures, and is invoked by
typing the command THERMO at the DOS prompt.  (For higher speed, with 
mathematics co-processor, use THERMOM.)  

	For further information, see HELP in the program.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

        THERMO MAY RUN TOO FAST ON PENTIUM OR HIGHER PROCESSORS:
TO SLOW DOWN SEARCH PARTICLES FOR MODES (ii) AND (iii) ABOVE, JUST GO TO
"RUN TIME OPTIONS MENU" AND SET "SNAIL TRAIL" TO MAX LENGTH OF 99 (NOT 0).  


